        "id": 214095,
        "name": "Ameena",
        "username": "Ameena",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/{size}/1907_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-01-29T14:49:49.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Hi, welcome to the forum :). Wow, that's a lot of links. I don't really have the time or inclination to go through them right now, but I have played Path of Exile. Last time was probably a couple of years ago, though - I know the game has changed a lot since then. It was good fun, though the end game stuff got pretty ridiculous - I was playing through with a friend and we did most of the late-game bosses by just zerging it, running in and getting off maybe one or two attacks before the boss would vaguely glance in our direction and insta-kill us. Repeat for, like, an hour and a half :P. And the exp loss on death at Merciless difficulty made it almost not worth attempting to level any more - you could spend an hour carefully grinding your way up the exp bar, and then lose all of it (and then some) to one single death. Not fun.</p><p>But apart from that, good game :). I like the way the skills and stuff work.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:45:12.160Z",
